model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-09-30
  start 2021-01-01
  end 2064-12-31
  use a = "../A" sha256 "3b42c3ad9491ce2cbb869aa0708959030d7e547e7dd608428ff5a32d29caf45c"
  use b = "../B" sha256 "2659269ab10c983b86538ea1103f4af5ff9fb829a4af1809944da1de8df3715c"
  use d = "../D" sha256 "2738c6dbbe7039e21e4f92c713f0835a9aa134365f6af9ea2e34caa5b0e47b11"
  note "Household E1 of the case set (tmp/cases/E1/story.md): Halina's family, households A (Ania and Tomek Lis), B (Piotr Sowa and Ola Wilk) and D (Halina Sowa) read together, in tally 2. It is a joint model (L §6.1): each household is a member, imported closed and unchanged under its prefix, a (households/A), b (households/B) and d (households/D); this directory holds only the family's own items and asks. Amounts are in DUK, the dukat of Lenia, of 100 orts, which the members declare (L §6.1, Currencies); B's florens are B's own."
  note "Each member is its household's directory tree, the law parts it reads copied into its own law/ (L §6.1: a law used by several realities is copied in, never linked; the reality is one directory tree): A/law holds the 27 parts its header names, B/law the 33 its header names, D/law all 63 of cases/law/, which D's own runs load. The copies are byte for byte cases/law/'s, so the members copy the same versions of each shared part (L §6.1, Shared law). The households' own runs still name cases/law/ and never their law/ (O:E1-1)."
  note "Each member's pin is of the canonical kind (E §3.1 step 1, L §2.4): the sha256 of its files' canonical reprints, taken in the order of their paths under it, as the reference interpreter computes it by default; L §2.4's last key (GD-28) settles the order of a version's same item beside the row of its target and keys (B/records/cis-2025.tally, D/records.tally), so B and D reprint too (O:E1-1)"
  note "On, start and end are the family's own: on is the latest member's (D's 2026-09-30), the run spans the members' (A's start 2021-01-01, D's end 2064-12-31). Every ask states its own law date and cut."
  note "No same line. The households state no kind, thing, row or movement in common: where they meet (story.md, the table) one side derives and another states or shows. Zbigniew's estate, its shares and its payouts are D's derivation (d.payout, d.deposit); Piotr's payout is B's Cis savings row (b.savr[s20250616a]) and B-D27; Ania's is A's A-D36 (a.estate_paid) and the row of her Wrzos export that E1 writes as an observation (e1_wrz). E1-01's checks hold each derivation against what the heir's household states and shows. Halina's gifts to Ania are A's alone (a.acq): D's text holds no row of them."
  note "The people. Each household keys its own: A's spouse index (ania, tomek), B's kind persons (piotr, ola), D's heir index (halina, piotr, anna, marta, jakub). A key of an index is no thing, so no same line can say that A's ania is D's anna (L §6.1: a same side is a kind, a thing, a row or a movement); E1's index e1_person names the six, and each rule of e1_worth reads the member's own key (O:E1-7)."

source e1_story "The family's own account: who is in which household, where the households meet, what happened (tmp/cases/E1/story.md)"

source e1_questions "The family's questions (tmp/cases/E1/questions.md)"

source e1_d_d07 "D-D07 · Agreement dividing the estate of Zbigniew Sowa (extract) (tmp/cases/D/docs/D-D07.md)"

source e1_b_d27 "B-D27 · Notary · estate of Zbigniew Sowa: payout to Piotr Sowa (tmp/cases/B/docs/B-D27.md)"

source e1_wrz_ania "Bank Wrzos, account history of Anna Lis's savings account LN61 1140 2004 0000 3402 9921 5503, 2025-06-02 .. 2025-12-31 (tmp/cases/A/records/wrz-ania-savings-2025.csv)"
